-->\n\n**Intent:** `commit_tactic`  \n**Payload:** `call (equ_cc n0 mr0 ms0).`\n\n---\n\nNow `n0`, `mr0`, `ms0` are all logical variables in context, exactly matching `equ_cc`'s three parameters. Now the `call` can take pure terms.\n","views/Tree_0_1_1/thinking/turn_020.md":"# Tree-0.1.1 \u00b7 turn 20 \u00b7 commit_tactic\n\n<!-- session 04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929 \u00b7 2026-06-04T17:44:28.967Z -->\n\n**Intent:** `commit_tactic`  \n**Payload:** `wp.`\n\n---\n\nBoth guards resolved \u2014 no `if`s left. Now consume the trailing deterministic assignments (`x3`, `r1`, `r20`, `ROout` update) so that `r6` becomes the last left sample, ready to couple with the right's `t`.\n","views/Tree_0_1_1/thinking/turn_014.md":"# Tree-0.1.1 \u00b7 turn 14 \u00b7 commit_tactic\n\n<!-- session 04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929 \u00b7 2026-06-04T17:39:42.758Z -->\n\n**Intent:** `commit_tactic`  \n**Payload:** `wp.`\n\n---\n\nI had the direction wrong \u2014 EC reasons backward from the *last* statement, which is the deterministic `t <- poly1305 ...`, not the leading `r5` sample. Let me consume the trailing deterministic assignments with `wp` and see where it stops.\n","views/Tree_0_1_1/thinking/turn_005.md":"# Tree-0.1.1 \u00b7 turn 5 \u00b7 commit_tactic\n\n<!-- session 04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929 \u00b7 2026-06-04T17:33:39.347Z -->\n\n**Intent:** `commit_tactic`  \n**Payload:** `skip.`\n\n---\n\nThe `call` succeeded \u2014 the goal is now a pure logical implication (empty programs): the precondition must imply `equ_cc`'s precondition plus the post-implication. Let me reduce the empty-program equiv to its logical form.\n","views/Tree_0_1_1/thinking/turn_021.md":"# Tree-0.1.1 \u00b7 turn 21 \u00b7 commit_tactic\n\n<!-- session 04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929 \u00b7 2026-06-04T17:45:15.790Z -->\n\n**Intent:** `commit_tactic`  \n**Payload:** `rnd (fun (s0:poly_out) => s0 + poly1305_eval r10{1} (topol a0{1} c3{1})) (fun (t0:poly_out) => t0 - poly1305_eval r10{1} (topol a0{1} c3{1})).`\n\n---\n\nNow `r6` is the last left sample, `t` the right one. Since `oget m_L.[x5] = r6` and `mk_rs (ofpair(ofpair(r10, r6), e)) = (r10, r6)`, the left tag is `t{1} = poly1305 r10 r6 (topol a0 c3) = r6 + poly1305_eval r10 (topol a0 c3)`. I couple `r6 \u21a6 t` by the offset bijection `s \u21a6 s + poly1305_eval r10 (topol a0 c3)` (inverse subtracts), which is measure-preserving on the funiform/full `dpoly_out`.\n","views/Tree_0_1_1/thinking/turn_015.md":"# Tree-0.1.1 \u00b7 turn 15 \u00b7 commit_tactic\n\n<!-- session 04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929 \u00b7 2026-06-04T17:40:17.594Z -->\n\n**Intent:** `commit_tactic`  \n**Payload:** `rnd{1}.`\n\n---\n\n`wp` absorbed the trailing `if` into the postcondition as an if-then-else; now the last left statement is the `r4 <$ dextra_block` sample. Since `mk_rs (ofpair(r1, e)) = (r10, r20)` regardless of `e` (by `mk_rs_ofpair`), `r4` is irrelevant \u2014 I dispose it one-sided (now it *is* the last left sample, so `rnd{1}` applies).\n","views/Tree_0_1_1/thinking/turn_001.md":"# Tree-0.1.1 \u00b7 turn 1 \u00b7 commit_tactic\n\n<!-- session 04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929 \u00b7 2026-06-04T17:29:52.780Z -->\n\n**Intent:** `commit_tactic`  \n**Payload:** `call (equ_cc (p{1}.`1) mr0 ms0).`\n\n---\n\nI'll start by loading the proof intent tool, then read the current state to plan my divergent approach.\n\nThe current goal is the first part of the `seq 1 1`: relating `ChaCha(...).enc(k,n,p2)` on the left with `EncRnd.cc(n,p1)` on the right. This is *exactly* the statement of the local lemma `equ_cc`, and the parent's `exists*`/`elim*` of `SplitC2.I1.RO.m{1}` and `SplitC2.I2.RO.m{1}` into `mr0 ms0` was set up precisely to feed that lemma's `mr0 ms0` parameters. The parent's `transitivity{1}` was an over-lowering \u2014 the higher-layer move here is a direct `call` of the bridge lemma.\n","views/Tree_0_1_1/thinking/turn_011.md":"# Tree-0.1.1 \u00b7 turn 11 \u00b7 commit_tactic\n\n<!-- session 04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929 \u00b7 2026-06-04T17:36:26.594Z -->\n\n**Intent:** `commit_tactic`  \n**Payload:** `move=> &m0; skip; rewrite /SplitD.test /=; smt(@C).`\n\n---\n\nSide goal: prove `SplitD.test x` holds, i.e. `C.toint (C.ofintd 0) = 0` \u2014 true by the `C` subtype roundtrip for the in-range value `0`. Using the discovered idiom.\n","views/Tree_0_1_1/thinking/index.json":{"node":"Tree-0.1.1","discovery":"content_match","transcripts":["~/.claude/projects/<PROJECT>-tmp-wt-focus-skeleton/04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929.jsonl"],"turns":[{"turn":1,"intent":"commit_tactic","payload_key":"call (equ_cc (p{1}.`1) mr0 ms0).","thinking_chars":0,"text_chars":586,"session_id":"04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929","timestamp":"2026-06-04T17:29:52.780Z","file":"thinking/turn_001.md"},{"turn":2,"intent":"commit_tactic","payload_key":"exists* (p{1}.`1).","thinking_chars":0,"text_chars":638,"session_id":"04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929","timestamp":"2026-06-04T17:32:38.248Z","file":"thinking/turn_002.md"},{"turn":3,"intent":"commit_tactic","payload_key":"elim* => n0.","thinking_chars":0,"text_chars":121,"session_id":"04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929","timestamp":"2026-06-04T17:32:43.708Z","file":"thinking/turn_003.md"},{"turn":4,"intent":"commit_tactic","payload_key":"call (equ_cc n0 mr0 ms0).","thinking_chars":0,"text_chars":142,"session_id":"04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929","timestamp":"2026-06-04T17:32:48.764Z","file":"thinking/turn_004.md"},{"turn":5,"intent":"commit_tactic","payload_key":"skip.","thinking_chars":0,"text_chars":221,"session_id":"04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929","timestamp":"2026-06-04T17:33:39.347Z","file":"thinking/turn_005.md"},{"turn":6,"intent":"commit_tactic","payload_key":"move=> &1 &2; rewrite /check_plaintext /valid_topol /inv_cpa /=; smt().","thinking_chars":0,"text_chars":333,"session_id":"04d4a898-436e-4cd4-8612-694f24113929","timestamp":"2026-06-04T17:33:59.826Z","file":"thinking/turn_006.md"},{"turn":7,"intent":